  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_048 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) at 0.706 accuracy. The evidence strongly supports scvi_n200 as the best RNA encoder and imagenet_vit_l as the best image encoder. However, avgpool outperformed transformer only when paired with the linear pca_n2000 encoder (0.639 vs 0.573). With scvi_n200 producing richer, nonlinear latent representations and vit_l producing more structured visual features, a transformer aggregation could capture inter-profile attention patterns that simple averaging misses. This experiment tests whether the transformer aggregation, which underperformed with a linear encoder, can succeed with the learned nonlinear encoders. It is a logical exploitation of the best-known component choices while exploring the one remaining aggregation mechanism. Expected cost is moderate (~5-8 GPU hours), comparable to config_048's 4.82 hours, since transformer with these encoders should not be dramatically more expensive than avgpool (cf. config_024 at 6.61h vs config_003 at 10.60h). This is the best use of experiment 9: it has a realistic chance of exceeding 0.706 if nonlinear representations benefit from attention-based profile interaction, while keeping total budget well-controlled for the final experiment."
}

